payload.body:
examiner (round 1): approach for the exam of Task A.

Two guarded sims, extended at the end of each file before its sentinel, imports at fleet/tests/ depth only (leg (k)).

fleet/tests/test_run_engine_proof_runs.mjs — legs (a)-(h). The existing `scenario` rig cannot cann a fix reply's `concerns` (its fix arm always returns doneImpl) and hands the stub no runDir, so the new legs are built on `factsRun` (line ~1664), which takes a whole inner stub and yields { prompts, runDir, evs }. Thirteen runs:
(a) x2 — blocking issue naming `one.txt`, actor implementer / no actor key;
(b) x2 — `one.txt:7`, and the landing path with a `:12-14` suffix on a task with an examiner (that run also pins driver:finding BEFORE the driver:exam-rejected the same issue buys);
(c) x2 — a detail with no backticked path (sorted touch set: files ['one.txt','b.txt'] + a patch that also writes 'a.txt', so sorted != touchSetOf order) and a canned PASS (no driver:finding at all);
(d) x3 — state-exams/task-T1/s-0/{mutant.json,walls.json} written from the impl stub into the run dir, killed false / true / mutant.json absent;
(e) — a toggle EXAM (red first run, green on the re-run, marker file in the task clone; the examiner's base probe runs in its own clone so it is unaffected) beside an implementer DONE_WITH_CONCERNS carrying 'plan-defect: leg (a) cannot pass';
(f) — an always-red exam, a fix reply DONE_WITH_CONCERNS carrying 'exam: case (b) cannot pass for any output', a round-1 reviewer blocking on the landing path;
(g) x2 — the same shape with a canned exam:T1:2 that writes nothing (clean) and one that rewrites the file (nothing appended);
(h) — the third Run: as an assertion too: the literal "kind: 'driver:finding'" read out of fleet/run-engine.mjs, count >= 2.

The captured headSha every evidence.against is pinned against is read out of the engine's own review prompt ('\nHEAD: <40 hex>'), not out of a clone re-read.

fleet/tests/test_run_engine_state_handshake.mjs — legs (i) and (j): two runs of its own `driveRun`, one posting an expected path the captured tree lacks, one posting a three-element content, asserting the handshake:finding row's paths/evidence and the no-key shape. The producer's captured headSha is recorded in the stub at impl dispatch (nothing commits between that and the capture's rev-parse).

Expected red at BASE for exactly one reason: kind: 'driver:finding' and kind: 'driver:finding-refuted' occur zero times in fleet/run-engine.mjs, and handshake:finding rows carry neither paths nor evidence.
